            <ArticleTitle>[Computerized tomography aspects of amiodarone poisoning].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>222-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Amiodarone, an antiarrhythmic drug, may cause pulmonary toxicity with typical high-attenuation-pleuro-parenchymal lesions and increased attenuation of liver and spleen. Characteristic CT findings are diagnostically significant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
